{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n \"Work Item|WorkItem|queuedWork|AC-2.7|AC-2.8|AC-3.6|AC-5.4|TC-2.6|TC-2.7|TC-2.9|TC-3.3|TC-3.6|TC-3.8|TC-5.4\" packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/epic.md packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/coverage.md packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/team-impl-log.md'","aggregated_output":"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/team-impl-log.md:157:- Story 4: pure transition fn golden per rule table; transition-then-stamp order; corruption check once at state load; gap messages null forever; corrupt fixture = one sanctioned below-SDK write; completes TC-4.4. AC-3.6/work halves deferred to S5 (close paths simply don't call queue; nothing stubbed).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/team-impl-log.md:158:- Story 5: work-queue util domain-blind, no public SDK surface; kind gate prompt->prompt_smoothing, tool_result->tool_result_summary (messages), turn close->turn_derivation (turns); ids w-<sourceId>-<kind>; gated on recorded. Named exit step: WorkItemRecord field-by-field shape review vs epic contract table, recorded in receipt. Closes full epic TC table.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/team-impl-log.md:160:- Coverage: 37/37 ACs, 33/33 TCs single-owner; debts: TC-1.4 S1->S2; TC-4.4 corruption S2->S4; TC-3.3/3.6 work halves + TC-3.8 count S4->S5; TC-5.4 clause ladder S2-S5; AC-4.6 rollback ladder S2-S5.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/epic.md:142:- **AC-2.7**: The batch result reports, per event: recorded or skipped, and for recorded message-producing events the created message id; plus any turn transitions the batch caused and any work items it queued.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/epic.md:143:- **AC-2.8**: A `user_prompt` message durably queues prompt-smoothing work and a `tool_result` message durably queues tool-result-summary work, each owned by `messages`, in the same atomic operation that records the batch.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/epic.md:153:- **TC-2.6** (AC-2.7): Result for a mixed batch names each event's outcome, the message ids created, the turn transitions, and the queued work items.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/epic.md:154:- **TC-2.7** (AC-2.8): A batch with a prompt and a tool result → one `messages`-owned work item for prompt smoothing and one for tool-result summary, readable from the queue with `queued` status and correct source references.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/epic.md:156:- **TC-2.9** (AC-2.8): Kinds that carry no message-level derivation (assistant text, thinking, runtime note) queue nothing.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/epic.md:182:- **AC-3.6**: Closing a turn — by either close path — durably queues that turn's derivation work, owned by `turns`, before the intake call returns.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/epic.md:191:- **TC-3.3** (AC-3.4, 3.6): Prompt, activity, `turn_end` → turn closed; a `turns`-owned work item for that turn readable with `queued` status.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/epic.md:194:- **TC-3.6** (AC-3.6): Close via implicit path (new prompt) → turn-derivation work item present, same contract as the explicit path.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/epic.md:196:- **TC-3.8** (AC-3.3): A single batch containing `prompt, text, prompt, text, turn_end` → two closed turns, correct membership in each, two turn-derivation work items.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/epic.md:243:- **AC-5.4**: A skipped event causes no side effects: no duplicate message, no turn transition, no work item.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/epic.md:251:- **TC-5.4** (AC-5.4): A resent batch containing a recorded `user_prompt` and a recorded `turn_end` → turn count and turn states unchanged; work-item count unchanged.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/epic.md:332:| `queuedWork` | array | Each: `{ workItemId, owner, kind, sourceRef }` (shapes below) |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/epic.md:344:### Work Item (the Epic 02 seam)\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/epic.md:384:1. Work-item granularity at turn close: one `turn_derivation` item, or one per derived artifact? (Shape is fixed by the Work Item contract; count is design's call.)\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/epic.md:432:**Flows/ACs covered:** AC-2.2 through AC-2.6, including AC-2.5 full tool-result preservation; AC-5.4's no-duplicate-message clause.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/epic.md:441:**Flows/ACs covered:** Flow 3 except AC-3.6 — AC-3.1 through AC-3.5, AC-3.7 through AC-3.9; completes AC-4.7.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/epic.md:446:**Delivers:** Durable work items: message-level (prompt smoothing, tool-result summary, owned by `messages`) queued as qualifying messages land; turn-level (owned by `turns`) queued at both close paths; work-item read-back; the batch result complete with `queuedWork`.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/epic.md:450:**Flows/ACs covered:** AC-2.7, AC-2.8, AC-3.6; AC-5.4's no-work-item clause.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/epic.md:481:| AC-2.7 | TC-2.6 | 5 |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/epic.md:482:| AC-2.8 | TC-2.7, TC-2.9 | 5 |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/epic.md:486:| AC-3.3 | TC-3.2, TC-3.8 | 4 |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/epic.md:487:| AC-3.4 | TC-3.3 | 4 |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/epic.md:489:| AC-3.6 | TC-3.3, TC-3.6 | 5 |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/epic.md:503:| AC-5.4 | TC-5.4 | 2, 3, 5 |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/coverage.md:24:| AC-2.7 | Story 5 | TC-2.6 | Stories 2–4 populate the result incrementally |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/coverage.md:25:| AC-2.8 | Story 5 | TC-2.7, TC-2.9 | — |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/coverage.md:29:| AC-3.3 | Story 4 | TC-3.2, TC-3.8 | TC-3.8's work-item count is Story 5's |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/coverage.md:30:| AC-3.4 | Story 4 | TC-3.3 (transition half) | — |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/coverage.md:32:| AC-3.6 | **Story 5** | TC-3.3, TC-3.6 (work halves) | Story 4 (close paths work; queueing absent by design) |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/coverage.md:46:| AC-5.4 | Story 2 | TC-5.4 | Clause ladder: Stories 3–5 (below) |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/coverage.md:59:| TC-3.3 / TC-3.6 work halves | Story 4 | Story 5 | AC-3.6: close paths queue `turn_derivation` (Story 4 ships working closes with no queueing; Story 5 adds the call) |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/coverage.md:60:| TC-3.8 work-item count | Story 4 | Story 5 | Two `turn_derivation` items from the multi-turn batch |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/coverage.md:62:**TC-5.4 clause ladder** (skipped events cause no side effects — each clause asserted when its record kind exists):\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/coverage.md:95:  assemble result during walk ................. S2 (messageIds S3, transitions S4, queuedWork S5)\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/coverage.md:109:- **Future-boundary notes:** the work-queue util gains no public SDK surface (read-back through owning domains only — Epic 02 consumes the seam, doesn't widen it). Read-back operations here are the deliberate embryo of Epic 04's inspection, minimal and ordered, no search. Registry cached stats deferred to a later epic. The `WorkItemRecord` shape review against the epic's contract table is Story 5's named exit step because Epic 02 builds on it.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
